#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Git v2.49 Release Notes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "UI, Workflows & Features"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:8
msgid "Completion script updates for zsh"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:13
msgid ""
"\"git pack-objects\" and its wrapper \"git repack\" learned an option to use "
"an alternative path-hash function to improve delta-base selection to produce "
"a packfile with deeper history than window size."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:16
msgid ""
"\"git gc\" learned the \"--expire-to\" option and passes it down to "
"underlying \"git repack\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:21
msgid ""
"\"[help] autocorrect = 1\" used to be a way to say \"please wait for 0.1 "
"second after suggesting a typofix of the command name before running that "
"command\"; now it means \"yes, if there is a plausible typofix for the "
"command name, please run it immediately\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:24
msgid ""
"\"git clone\" learned to make a shallow clone for a single commit that is "
"not necessarily be at the tip of any branch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:28
msgid ""
"Lazy-loading missing files in a blobless clone on demand is costly as it "
"tends to be one-blob-at-a-time.  \"git backfill\" is introduced to help "
"bulk-download necessary files beforehand."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:32
msgid ""
"\"git push --atomic --porcelain\" used to ignore failures from the other "
"side, losing the error status from the child process, which has been "
"corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:35
msgid ""
"\"git rev-list --missing=\" learned to accept \"print-info\" that gives "
"known details expected of the missing objects, like path and type."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:37
msgid "Comes with an updated \"gitk\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:40
msgid ""
"The documentation of \"git commit\" and \"git rebase\" now refer to commit "
"titles as such, not \"subject\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:43
msgid ""
"The value of \"uname -s\" is by default sent over the wire as a part of the "
"\"version\" capability."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:45
msgid "\"git refs migrate\" can optionally be told not to migrate the reflog."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:48
msgid ""
"The netrc support (via the cURL library) for the HTTP transport has been "
"re-enabled."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:51
msgid ""
"Removal of \".git/branches\" and \".git/remotes\" support in the "
"BreakingChanges document has been further clarified."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:54
msgid ""
"What happens to submodules during merge has been documented in a bit more "
"detail."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:57
#, no-wrap
msgid "Performance, Internal Implementation, Development Support etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:60
msgid "More -Wsign-compare fixes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:62
msgid "meson-based build now supports the unsafe-sha1 build knob."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:65
msgid "The meson-based build procedure covers contrib/ and other places as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:69
msgid ""
"The code to check LSan results has been simplified and made more robust.  "
"(merge 164a2516eb jk/lsan-race-ignore-false-positive later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:72
msgid ""
"More code paths have a repository passed through the callchain, instead of "
"assuming the primary the_repository object."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:74
msgid "Move a few more unit tests to the clar test framework."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:77
msgid ""
"Introduce a new API to visit objects in batches based on a common path, or "
"by type."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:82
msgid ""
"Following the procedure we established to introduce breaking changes for Git "
"3.0, allow an early opt-in for removing support of $GIT_DIR/branches/ and "
"$GIT_DIR/remotes/ directories to configure remotes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:85
msgid ""
"The code paths to interact with zlib has been cleaned up in preparation for "
"building with zlib-ng."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:87
msgid "Foreign language interface for Rust into our code base has been added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:90
msgid ""
"All the documentation .txt files have been renamed to .adoc to help content "
"aware editors."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:92
msgid "\"git difftool\" code clean-up."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:95
msgid ""
"Rename processing in the recursive merge backend has seen a micro "
"optimization."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:99
msgid ""
"The path.[ch] API takes an explicit repository parameter passed throughout "
"the callchain, instead of relying on the_repository singleton instance."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:101
msgid "Large-object promisor protocol extension has been introduced."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:104
msgid ""
"The editorconfig file is updated to tell us that bash scripts are similar to "
"general Bourne shell scripts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:107
msgid ""
"Meson-based build procedure forgot to build some docs, which has been "
"corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:110
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fixes since v2.48"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:115
msgid ""
"\"git submodule\" learned various ways to spell the same option, "
"e.g. \"--branch=B\" can be spelled \"--branch B\" or \"-bB\".  (merge "
"b86f0f9071 re/submodule-parse-opt later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:120
msgid ""
"Tweak the help text used for the option value placeholders by parse-options "
"API so that translations can customize the \"<>\" placeholder signal "
"(e.g. \"--option=<value>\").  (merge 5b34dd08d0 as/long-option-help-i18n "
"later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:125
msgid ""
"CI jobs gave sporadic failures, which turns out that that the object "
"finalization code was giving an error when it did not have to.  (merge "
"d7fcbe2c56 ps/object-collision-check later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:130
msgid ""
"The code to compute \"unique\" name used git_rand() which can fail or get "
"stuck; the callsite does not require cryptographic security.  Introduce the "
"\"insecure\" mode and use it appropriately.  (merge 0b4f8afef6 "
"ps/reftable-get-random-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:134
msgid ""
"A misconfigured \"fsck.skiplist\" configuration variable was not diagnosed "
"as an error, which has been corrected.  (merge ca7158076f "
"jt/fsck-skiplist-parse-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:138
msgid ""
"Extended SHA-1 expression parser did not work well when a branch with an "
"unusual name (e.g. \"foo{bar\") is involved.  (merge 191f0c8db2 "
"en/object-name-with-funny-refname-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:142
msgid ""
"The meson build procedure looked for the 'version-def.h' file in a wrong "
"directory, which has been corrected.  (merge 4771501c0a "
"tc/meson-use-our-version-def-h later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:146
msgid ""
"The meson build procedure for Documentation/technical/ hierarchy was missing "
"necessary dependencies, which has been corrected.  (merge 1dca492edd "
"sj/meson-doc-technical-dependency-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:151
msgid ""
"The \"instaweb\" bound only to local IP address without \"--local\" and to "
"all addresses with \"--local\", which was the other way around, when using "
"Python's http.server class, which has been corrected.  (merge 76baf97fa1 "
"ak/instaweb-python-port-binding-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:155
msgid ""
"Document that it is insecure to use Personal Access Tokens, which some "
"hosting providers take as username/password, embedded in URLs.  (merge "
"a90ff409f0 mh/doc-credential-helpers-with-pat later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:160
msgid ""
"The help text from \"git $cmd -h\" appear on the standard output for some "
"$cmd and the standard error for others.  The built-in commands have been "
"fixed to show them on the standard output consistently.  (merge f66d1423f5 "
"jc/show-usage-help later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:164
msgid ""
"The meson-driven build is now aware of \"git-subtree\" housed in "
"contrib/subtree hierarchy.  (merge 8454b42f94 ps/build-meson-subtree later "
"to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:168
msgid ""
"It was possible for \"git unpack-objects\" and \"git index-pack\" to make an "
"unaligned access, which has been corrected.  (merge 98046591b9 "
"jk/pack-header-parse-alignment-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:172
msgid ""
"The \"cache\" credential back-end did not handle authtype correctly, which "
"has been corrected.  (merge 0b43274850 "
"mh/credential-cache-authtype-request-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:176
msgid ""
"\"git branch --sort=...\" and \"git for-each-ref --format=... --sort=...\" "
"did not work as expected with some atoms, which has been corrected.  (merge "
"c5490ce9d1 rs/ref-fitler-used-atoms-value-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:180
msgid ""
"reflog entries for symbolic ref updates were broken, which has been "
"corrected.  (merge 3519492430 kn/reflog-symref-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:185
msgid ""
"The trace2 code was not prepared to show a configuration variable that is "
"set to true using the valueless true syntax, which has been corrected.  "
"(merge 2fd367cf63 am/trace2-with-valueless-true later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:190
msgid ""
"The \"git refs migrate\" command did not migrate the reflog for refs/stash, "
"which is the contents of the stashes, which has been corrected.  (merge "
"a0bea0978f ps/reflog-migration-with-logall-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:194
msgid ""
"Doc and short-help text for \"show-index\" has been clarified to stress that "
"the command reads its data from the standard input.  (merge 49edce4ff9 "
"jc/show-index-h-update later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:199
msgid ""
"The API around choosing to use unsafe variant of SHA-1 implementation has "
"been updated in an attempt to make it harder to abuse.  (merge 04292c3796 "
"tb/unsafe-hash-cleanup later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:202
msgid ""
"Fix bugs in an earlier attempt to fix \"git refs migration\".  (merge "
"f11f0a5a2d kn/reflog-migration-fix-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:208
msgid ""
"The code path used when \"git fetch\" fetches from a bundle file closed the "
"same file descriptor twice, which sometimes broke things unexpectedly when "
"the file descriptor was reused, which has been corrected.  (merge 9a84794ad8 "
"js/bundle-unbundle-fd-reuse-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:213
msgid ""
"\"git init\" to reinitialize a repository that already exists cannot change "
"the hash function and ref backends; such a request is silently ignored now.  "
"(merge 7e88640cd1 ps/setup-reinit-fixes later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:218
msgid ""
"\"git apply\" internally uses unsigned long for line numbers and uses "
"strtoul() to parse numbers on the hunk headers.  It however forgot to check "
"parse errors.  (merge a206058fda pw/apply-ulong-overflow-check later to "
"maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:224
msgid ""
"Two CI tasks, whitespace check and style check, work on the difference from "
"the base version and the version being checked, but the base was computed "
"incorrectly in GitLab CI in some cases, which has been corrected.  (merge "
"acc4fb302b jt/gitlab-ci-base-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:229
msgid ""
"\"git repack --keep-unreachable\" to send unreachable objects to the main "
"pack \"git repack -ad\" produces did not work when there is no existing "
"packs, which has been corrected.  (merge 414c82300a "
"ps/repack-keep-unreachable-in-unpacked-repo later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:233
msgid ""
"Going into a secondary worktree and asking \"is the main worktree bare?\" "
"did not work correctly when per-worktree configuration option was in use, "
"which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:238
msgid ""
"Fetching into a bare repository incorrectly assumed it always used a mirror "
"layout when deciding to update remote-tracking HEAD, which has been "
"corrected.  (merge 93dc16483a bf/fetch-set-head-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:241
msgid ""
"A thunderbird helper script lost its bashism.  (merge 59d26bd961 "
"bc/contrib-thunderbird-patch-inline-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:245
msgid ""
"The -G/-S options to the \"diff\" family of commands caused us to hit a "
"BUG() when they get no values; they have been corrected.  (merge a620046b29 "
"bc/diff-reject-empty-arg-to-pickaxe later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:249
msgid ""
"\"git merge-tree --stdin\" has been improved (including a workaround for a "
"deadlock).  (merge 6a9ae81015 pw/merge-tree-stdin-deadlock-fix later to "
"maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:254
msgid ""
"Correct the default target in Documentation/Makefile, and future-proof all "
"Makefiles from similar breakages by declaring the default target (which "
"happens to be \"all\") upfront.  (merge 5309c1e9fb "
"ad/set-default-target-in-makefiles later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:258
msgid ""
"\"git check-mailmap\" used to segfault when queried without human readable "
"name.  (merge bb60c52131 jk/check-mailmap-wo-name-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:260
msgid "Support for renaming of symbolic links on Windows has been improved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:264
msgid ""
"\"git rebase -i\" failed to allow rewording an empty commit that has been "
"fast-forwarded.  (merge af8fc7be10 pw/rebase-i-ff-empty-commit later to "
"maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:268
msgid ""
"The use of \"paste\" command for aggregating the test results have been "
"corrected.  (merge ce98863204 dk/test-aggregate-results-paste-fix later to "
"maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.49.0.adoc:288
msgid ""
"Other code cleanup, docfix, build fix, etc.  (merge ddb5287894 "
"jk/t7407-use-test-grep later to maint).  (merge 21e1b44865 "
"aj/difftool-config-doc-fix later to maint).  (merge 6a63995335 "
"mh/gitattr-doc-markup-fix later to maint).  (merge 43850dcf9c "
"sk/unit-test-hash later to maint).  (merge 4ad47d2de3 "
"jc/cli-doc-option-and-config later to maint).  (merge 2d0ff147e5 "
"jp/t8002-printf-fix later to maint).  (merge 69666e6746 "
"ja/doc-restore-markup-update later to maint).  (merge d11d003ba5 "
"sk/strlen-returns-size_t later to maint).  (merge 77b2d29e91 "
"ja/doc-notes-markup-updates later to maint).  (merge 6979bf6f8f "
"jk/combine-diff-cleanup later to maint).  (merge 8705c9bd13 "
"kn/pack-write-with-reduced-globals later to maint).  (merge 087740d65a "
"ps/leakfixes-0129 later to maint).  (merge 6bba6f604b jp/doc-trailer-config "
"later to maint).  (merge f1cc562b77 lo/t7603-path-is-file-update later to "
"maint).  (merge 45761988ac en/doc-renormalize later to maint).  (merge "
"832f56f06a jc/doc-boolean-synonyms later to maint).  (merge 3eeed876a9 "
"ac/doc-http-ssl-type-config later to maint).  (merge c268e3285d "
"jc/breaking-changes-early-adopter-option later to maint).  (merge 0d03fda6a5 "
"pb/doc-follow-remote-head later to maint)."
msgstr ""
